# Phase 5 EOL policy decision (P5 Task 7 — finalizes the "revisit" this file used to defer).
# Broadened from `*.svelte` alone to every text extension this migration actually authors,
# proven a content no-op by a node Buffer (byte 13) CR scan over every tracked file BEFORE this
# rule was added (raw counts in docs/superpowers/sdd/P5-task-7-report.md): *.svelte/*.ts/*.js/
# *.css/*.scss/*.html were all already 100% CR-free.
#
# `*.json` is deliberately NOT added: 21 of 57 tracked .json files already contain CR, scattered
# across six unrelated pre-migration directories (docs/assets, src/lib/games/*/static,
# static/locales, static/updates.json, test-songs/, test/inputs/) — renormalizing them is out of
# scope for this task, and test/fixtures/ (immutable) is itself all .json, so a blanket json rule
# is the wrong shape of risk to take here. Revisit with a narrower, path-scoped rule if a future
# phase wants LF-locked JSON.
#
# `*.md` and `*.yml` are added, with the handful of pre-existing CRLF outliers carved out by path
# since each is a single well-identified non-authored file, not migration content:
# - static/assets/audio/sky/SFX_*/README.md (8 files): bundled third-party asset attribution.
# - test-songs/ThingsToTest.md: pre-migration legacy test note.
# - .github/FUNDING.yml: GitHub-native sponsor-button config, not a CI workflow file.
#
# No blanket `* text=auto`: that would reclassify every binary/asset path under static/ and
# test/fixtures/ — fixtures are immutable.
*.svelte text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.scss text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
static/assets/audio/sky/SFX_*/README.md -text
test-songs/ThingsToTest.md -text
*.yml text eol=lf
.github/FUNDING.yml -text
